			<div class="content" id="post-content-1488085">
									

<p>The idea is that they have to have been &quot;originally placed&quot; before 1860. Apparently whatever decides that this train will interact with a track dosn't mind if you move that track around, but it won't accept bits of track that have been modified beyond simple translation.</p>
<p>It's admittedly something of a practicality hack, but it makes some sense if you consider that there's such a thing as &quot;movable track&quot; in the first place, such as roundhouses and switches.</p>

							</div>

								
